        <item>
            <title>0.18.15</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:36:27 +0100</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.18.15</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.18.15</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<h2>What's new in 0.18.15</h2>
<ul>
<li>**Function keys** — open any menu with an F key, for when your hand sits higher: its own card in Settings, one key per menu. &quot;Mirror on the right&quot; makes F12 to F9 open what F1 to F4 open, for the other hand. The card tells you what your Mac&#x27;s top row does and where the switch for it is.</li>
<li>**⌥ Option is a menu key like any other** — the dedicated alternates key is gone. The second actions come by tapping the menu&#x27;s own key again and holding, by a double click on the centre, or by the twist. A double tap&#x27;s second press shows them at once; a hold shows them after a quarter second.</li>
<li>**Replace by dropping** — drop a pill on a taken seat and it replaces at once; the card offers Undo, which puts the occupant back and the newcomer in your hand again. A full folder says so instead of taking the pill.</li>
<li>**Suggestion cards for links, files and shortcuts** — a copied link shows the page&#x27;s title and icon; a copied file or folder, or a path on the clipboard, is offered as a pill; an app&#x27;s own shortcut you press on two days gets a card with its keys as key caps.</li>
<li>**The alternates flip no longer lags** — switching to the second actions and back redraws nothing it does not need to.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
